# The container's schedule, run by supercronic (see Dockerfile). Two jobs. Edit an
# expression and rebuild. The 15-minute line is also assumed by the healthcheck's
# three-missed-runs allowance (healthcheck.sh); the betas line is not.
#
# There is no market-hours window on the check. `alert check` exits without fetching a
# quote outside a session and `dashboard --skip-unchanged` fingerprints before it
# fetches, so an overnight run costs nothing, and `ops pull` should drain queued
# dashboard edits whether or not the market is open (see docs/SCHEDULING.md).
#
# The betas job (run-beta.sh) refreshes /shared/betas.json for another container. The
# options-spread report publishes at 07:45 and 13:25 Denver, so these run about 20
# and 40 minutes after each publish: a symbol added to underlyings.txt has a beta
# within a day, and none in the first report that lists it. It is off the check's
# heartbeat and ping on purpose (see run-beta.sh).
#
# Times are in TZ (default America/Denver). The 15-minute line doesn't care; the betas
# line does.
*/15 * * * * /app/docker/run-check.sh
5 8,14 * * 1-5  /app/docker/run-beta.sh
